<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">warrior-routes</ansi>

The warrior lineage splits at level 10 into a protector of faith, a brawler
or a protector of blood. They all fight in the front rank; the Knight and the
Blackguard also heal.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Knight (good)</ansi>

  10 Lay on Hands       heals itself or an adjacent ally for half a Minor Heal;
                        takes its turn, no chant or mana; 2 uses per rest
  15 Second wind        3 uses per rest
  20 Shield of faith    +5 block chance while guarding a ward
  25 Staunch hands      Lay on Hands also stops bleeding

  <ansi fg="yellow-bold">Paladin</ansi> (30): Lay on Hands is a full Minor Heal and removes a harmful status;
  Aura of Resolve (allies in its row take 10% less damage; auras don't stack
  within a row); 4 uses; Smite (+50% against undead and demons); Rallying aura
  (5% to the rest of the company); Far hands (any ally in reach); Divine shield
  (once a battle it ignores the next blow; 5 uses).

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Mercenary (neutral)</ansi>

  10 Hard tackle        Tackle succeeds 10 points more often, ready a round sooner
  15 Practiced hands    +2 Attack
  20 Pin down           a tackled foe stays down a round longer
  25 Hit while down     a tackled foe is also left exposed

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Blackguard (evil)</ansi>

  10 Blood Oath         a melee blow that lands heals the most hurt ally for half
                        the damage; 3 blows a battle; the foe it wounds has -3
                        Attack against its allies that round and the next
  15 Deeper oath        4 blows a battle
  20 Fearful wounds     the wounded foe has -5 Attack
  25 Deepest oath       5 blows a battle

  <ansi fg="yellow-bold">Dread Knight</ansi> (30): Blood Oath heals 75%, Aura of Dread (foes aimed at it have -1
  Attack), Spreading oath (a second ally heals half as much), up to 7 blows,
  Terror (its critical hits that land also stagger the target, which loses its
  next action), and at 60 Blood Oath heals 100%.

Lay on Hands uses come back with a rest (a camp rest, an inn).

